Native video decoding support bundled with codec_vis.

native/ contains the H.265 parser, Vulkan Video decoder, and required headers.
The sources are built as C++23 objects. Include paths and namespaces are scoped
under native_video, and runtime configuration uses CODEC_VIS environment names.
native/SOURCE.json records repository-relative snapshot paths and SHA-256 hashes.
No separate project checkout is needed to build this code.

HEVC SCC uses the native parser and direct Vulkan Video submission, with
same-device timeline synchronization and CPU image readback in gui/scc_decode.cpp.
SCC does not use libavcodec for parsing, decoding, or surface download.
Other video decoder integrations use in-process libraries for codec parsing,
hardware submission, and synchronized CPU surface download.
